      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Edit cargo_embargo.json and run \u0027./crate_tool regenerate \u003ccrate name\u003e\u0027\n\nLet me explain the context here. We\u0027re now trying to use nsjail to build Trusty. To use nsjail, we need to bind-mount directories and `external/rust/android-crates-io` is one of them.\n\nI understand that it\u0027s expected to edit `cargo_embargo.json` for `Android.bp` integration, but I\u0027m not sure if it\u0027s what we really want here.\n\n* I think mounting only one directory `external/rust/android-crates-io` is much more efficient than mounting subdirectories one by one. That will easily bloat the command line of nsjail and affect performance negatively.\n* This is a one-time change and we won\u0027t need to maintain further, contrast to `cargo_embargo.json` approach.\n\nCan we land this as-is?",
      "parentUuid": "8d552f51_861adedf",
